  "purpose": "declared reposition, not a route: walk the hero to the centre of minimap cell 19:13 so a cold-start test can begin from the recorded v14 failing start of (78.4, 55.4). The owner asked for placements to be performed here rather than by hand, and a declared one-waypoint contract on the same guarded runner is both more accurate and more reproducible than a manual scene adjustment. Everything except the route identity and the single target is copied unchanged from route B v15, including the traversability mask and the final-approach commitment, so the reposition crosses the same cells with the same instrument that passes the route. Waypoints are [y, x] because the runner compares the first component against the localised row. The arrival gate is the contract's own 4.0 px, and the actual resting position is reported by the read-only cue check afterwards rather than assumed.",
